<Prose
  title="About — PDF tools that never see your files"
  description="Why this site exists, how it works, and why your files never leave your device."
  h1="About"
>
  <p>
    This site is a set of PDF tools with one defining property: every tool runs entirely in
    your browser. There is no upload step, no processing server, and no account. The same
    engine that powers professional PDF software runs on your own device through
    WebAssembly.
  </p>
  <p>
    It began as a small desktop application for converting PDFs to images. The desktop app
    is still available and uses the same rendering engine, so the output you get here is
    identical to it — this is tested automatically, pixel by pixel, on every change.
  </p>
  <h2>Why local processing matters</h2>
  <p>
    Most online PDF tools send your document to a server, process it there, and send the
    result back. That model requires you to trust a company with contracts, invoices,
    medical records — whatever you happen to convert. Local processing removes the question
    entirely: nothing is transmitted, so there is nothing to trust anyone with.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions and bug reports are welcome — see the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
